    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 8
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "## Hazelcast Cluster Overview\n\nOperational view of the AP Hazelcast cluster used by Simulator runs. It focuses on member availability, heap pressure, CPU/load, partitions, clients, and scrape/runtime health.\n\n**Key questions this dashboard answers:**\n- Is the expected number of members connected? *(Cluster Size, Members by Address)*\n- Are any members under CPU, heap, GC, or file descriptor pressure?\n- Are partitions balanced and migrations quiet during steady state?\n- Is Management Center exporting metrics for every member?\n\n**Filters:** **Cluster** selects the MC cluster. **Member** narrows member-level panels.\n\n**Simulator context:** use this dashboard during member or DC failover tests to watch the cluster size dip, partition migration activity, and recovery back to a balanced state."
      },
      "transparent": true
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "row",
